1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:20,320
There are very few places on Earth that are undiscovered and we have satellite photos of the most remote places on the planet.

2
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:31,916
But people are always interested in mythical lands, places that people say exist but no one has ever found.

3
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:37,920
Perhaps the most famous mythical place of all is Atlantis.

4
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:48,140
Some people say it is a city, others say it is an island and others call it a continent.

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:58,712
But whatever it is exactly, there is one thing that everyone agrees on: it is underneath the sea.

6
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:10,900
The Greek philosopher Plato was the first person to describe it and he suggested that one time, its people attacked Athens.

7
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:16,057
No one is sure exactly where Atlantis is.

8
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:21,860
Because of its name, some people think it is somewhere in the Atlantic Ocean.

9
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:28,000
Others say it’s in the Mediterranean Sea or in the Caribbean.

10
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:34,865
Agartha is another mythical place that is not on the land.

11
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:39,500
The legend says that it’s at the centre of our planet.

12
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:46,620
Like Atlantis, it is famous for its culture and educated society.

13
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:54,020
It was the inspiration for Jules Verne’s novel Journey to the Centre of the Earth.

14
00:01:55,080 --> 00:02:02,000
It tells the story of a group of travellers who go on an exciting adventure underground.

15
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:11,140
Many people have tried to find the entrance to Agartha, which they think is somewhere in Antarctica.

16
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:22,120
Some people believe that somewhere in South America there is a famous city of gold: El Dorado.

17
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:28,040
Many people tried to find it, but they weren’t successful.

18
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:39,231
El Dorado was originally the name of a person, a ruler of the ancient Colombian society called the Muisca.

19
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:44,160
He covered himself in gold powder every day.

20
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:51,886
There were legends in which people imagined that the whole city was made of gold.

21
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:59,000
Our final mythical land is an island called Thule.

22
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:07,400
The legend says that it is in the north of the Earth, somewhere between Norway and Iceland.

23
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:14,885
This is an area of the world that is completely dark for a lot of the year.

24
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:25,940
But the story goes that Thule is a place where a lot of delicious food grows and people are always happy.

25
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:32,340
The Roman poet Silius Italicus wrote about Thule.

26
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:37,860
In his story, the people living there are painted blue.
